    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WiLad">Wl lad</ref> 2.3</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="232" ed="#robertson"/>7 gif se Englisca nele hine werian mid orneste oððe mid gewitnesse, he ladige hine mid irene.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="233" ed="#robertson"/>And if the Englishman will not defend himself by combat or by compurgation, he shall clear himself by the ordeal of iron.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 232–233 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
    </body>
